  "executive_view": {
    "headline": "Capex broadened from accelerators into the full datacenter stack",
    "summary": "The eight-supplier panel shows accelerating revenue, orders or profitability across compute, foundry, memory, networking, power and cooling. Relationship evidence is strongest where suppliers name customers or counterparties; upstream revenue remains non-additive.",
    "analyst_conclusion": "The spend cycle broadened from accelerators into memory, networking and physical infrastructure, but the clearest disclosed customer exposure remains concentrated in NVIDIA, Arista and selected custom-silicon programs. Upstream foundry, HBM and cooling vendors show strong operating leverage, yet their revenue cannot be added to downstream supplier revenue because the same deployed system passes through multiple layers.",
    "decisive_metrics": [
      {
        "label": "Largest 2025 cash-capex base",
        "display": "Amazon $128.3bn",
        "raw": 128.32,
        "format": "USD billions, one decimal",
