      }
    ],
    "implications": [
      "Accelerator demand remains the first-order transmission channel: all four buyers publicly committed to NVIDIA Blackwell adoption or deployment.",
      "Memory and foundry profitability moved from cyclical recovery to AI-led expansion; the strongest 2026 quarterly margins are at SK hynix, Micron and TSMC, though periods and currencies differ.",
      "Networking has the clearest audited customer concentration: Arista directly quantifies Microsoft and Meta exposure.",
      "Power and cooling demand is visible in Eaton and Vertiv orders/backlog, but only Microsoft-Eaton and NVIDIA-Vertiv are included as named relationships; no unsupported hyperscaler-to-facility-supplier links are inferred."
    ],
    "change_conditions": [
      "A material slowdown in hyperscaler actual capex or a shift from owned infrastructure to lower-capital deployment models.",
      "Evidence that custom accelerators materially displace merchant GPUs faster than networking and memory content expands.",
      "Supplier backlog cancellations, weaker book-to-bill, or margin compression caused by capacity, pricing or mix."
    ],
